 tips=["Use a UV flashlight at night to spot scorpions on walls.",
       "Seal weep holes, door gaps and gaps around pipes.",
       "Move beds slightly away from walls and keep bedding off the floor.",
       "Shake out shoes and clothing left in garages."],
 topic=("Bark scorpions in Utah's Dixie",
        "<p>Arizona bark scorpions reach as far north as St. George, making it the one part of Utah where they're a common household pest. They climb walls and ceilings, squeeze through gaps the width of a credit card and glow under UV light. Control combines sealing gaps, removing rock piles and debris near the house, nighttime UV inspections and regular perimeter treatments. Sticky traps in garages and closets help track activity. See <a href=\"/services/spider-control/\">scorpion control</a> and <a href=\"/services/termite-inspection/\">termite inspection</a>.</p>"),
